1
00:00:04,922 --> 00:00:09,426
( operatic tenor bellowing):
♪ MORNING'S HERE ♪

2
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:12,262
♪ THE MORNING'S HERE ♪

3
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:14,974
♪ SUNSHINE IS HERE ♪

4
00:00:14,974 --> 00:00:16,099
♪ THE SKY IS CLEAR ♪

5
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:19,102
♪ THE MORNING'S HERE ♪

6
00:00:19,102 --> 00:00:20,312
♪ THE MORNING'S HERE... ♪

7
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:22,982
HEY!

8
00:00:22,982 --> 00:00:24,775
DO YOU HAVE TO DO THAT?

9
00:00:24,775 --> 00:00:26,986
IT'S SATURDAY!

10
00:00:26,986 --> 00:00:28,737
OH, COME ON.

11
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:30,739
MORNING'S HERE!

12
00:00:30,739 --> 00:00:34,493
♪ MORNING'S HERE ♪

13
00:00:34,493 --> 00:00:36,704
♪ THE MORNING'S HERE ♪

14
00:00:36,704 --> 00:00:39,456
♪ SUNSHINE IS HERE ♪

15
00:00:39,456 --> 00:00:42,376
♪ LA-DA-DA
DAH-DAH-DAH-DAH-DAH... ♪

16
00:00:42,376 --> 00:00:44,503
I HATE THIS APARTMENT!

17
00:00:44,503 --> 00:00:45,754
( door slams )

18
00:00:45,754 --> 00:00:47,798
I HATE THE COLOR OF THESE WALLS.

19
00:00:47,798 --> 00:00:50,049
I HATE THE FACT THIS PLACE
STILL SMELLS LIKE BIRD.

20
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:54,262
I HATE THAT SINGING GUY.

21
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:55,597
ARE YOU KIDDING?

22
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:57,808
I LOVE THAT GUY.

23
00:00:57,808 --> 00:01:00,602
♪ MORNING'S HERE ♪

24
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:01,603
♪ MORNING IS... ♪

25
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:04,523
STOP IT!

26
00:01:04,523 --> 00:01:05,524
I WILL KILL YOU.

27
00:01:07,108 --> 00:01:08,569
GOD.

28
00:01:08,569 --> 00:01:10,988
I HATE THE FACT
THAT MY ROOM IS SO SMALL.

29
00:01:10,988 --> 00:01:12,155
HEY, I HAVE ALL
THE SPACE I NEED.

30
00:01:12,155 --> 00:01:13,699
JUST DO WHAT I DID.

31
00:01:13,699 --> 00:01:15,617
MONICA, YOU DON'T EVEN
HAVE A BED.

32
00:01:15,617 --> 00:01:19,454
YOU SLEEP IN A BALL
ON THE FLOOR.

33
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:20,831
YOU KNOW WHAT?
I AM REALLY TIRED OF

34
00:01:20,831 --> 00:01:22,290
YOUR BELLYACHING, OKAY?

35
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:23,667
I'VE WORKED REALLY
HARD AT MAKING THIS

36
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:26,003
A NICE PLACE FOR US TO LIVE.

37
00:01:26,003 --> 00:01:27,004
I KNOW.

38
00:01:27,004 --> 00:01:28,005
I'M SO SORRY.

39
00:01:28,005 --> 00:01:29,798
I'M SORRY, OKAY?

40
00:01:29,798 --> 00:01:31,508
THIS IS A GREAT
APARTMENT.

41
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:33,343
SHUT UP! THIS
PLACE IS A HOLE!

42
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:45,856
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

43
00:01:45,856 --> 00:01:47,942
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

44
00:01:47,942 --> 00:01:51,028
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

45
00:01:51,028 --> 00:01:55,323
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

46
00:01:55,323 --> 00:01:57,409
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

47
00:01:57,409 --> 00:02:00,412
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

48
00:02:00,412 --> 00:02:04,165
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

49
00:02:04,165 --> 00:02:06,125
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

50
00:02:06,125 --> 00:02:09,170
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

51
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:11,090
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

52
00:02:11,090 --> 00:02:14,259
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

53
00:02:14,259 --> 00:02:17,805
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

54
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:32,319
OH, BLIMEY!
I STILL CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU'VE GOT AN EARRING.

55
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:33,779
I KNOW. WHO AM I:

56
00:02:33,779 --> 00:02:35,447
( English accent ):
DAVID BOWIE?

57
00:02:37,825 --> 00:02:39,076
HE DOES THAT?

58
00:02:39,076 --> 00:02:41,745
I DON'T KNOW. WHATEVER.

59
00:02:41,745 --> 00:02:44,498
I THINK IT MAKES YOU LOOK
REALLY DANGEROUS.

60
00:02:44,498 --> 00:02:47,542
OH, I KNOW.

61
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:48,752
YOU KNOW WHAT?

62
00:02:48,752 --> 00:02:50,087
I NEVER WOULD
HAVE GOTTEN THIS

63
00:02:50,087 --> 00:02:51,088
IF IT WEREN'T FOR YOU.

64
00:02:51,088 --> 00:02:52,965
NO, REALLY.

65
00:02:52,965 --> 00:02:56,593
WHEN I'M WITH YOU, I'M LIKE
THIS-THIS WHOLE OTHER GUY.

66
00:02:56,593 --> 00:02:58,512
I LOVE THAT GUY.

67
00:02:58,512 --> 00:03:00,639
I MEAN, I LOVE YOU,
TOO, A LOT

68
00:03:00,639 --> 00:03:03,142
BUT THAT GUY.

69
00:03:03,142 --> 00:03:04,225
I LOVE THAT GUY.

70
00:03:04,225 --> 00:03:05,435
I LOVE BOTH OF YOU.

71
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:06,478
YEAH?

72
00:03:08,147 --> 00:03:09,397
( sighs )

73
00:03:09,397 --> 00:03:12,609
I WISH I DIDN'T
HAVE TO GO.

74
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:13,944
THEN DON'T.

75
00:03:13,944 --> 00:03:15,278
STAY HERE.

76
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:16,321
JUST DON'T GO
SO SOON TO LONDON.

77
00:03:16,321 --> 00:03:18,197
JUST ONE MORE DAY.

78
00:03:18,197 --> 00:03:21,368
ROSS, PLEASE DON'T
DO THIS TO ME AGAIN.
ONE MORE DAY.

79
00:03:21,368 --> 00:03:22,744
I'D STAY IN A MINUTE

80
00:03:22,744 --> 00:03:24,454
BUT I'VE ALREADY MISSED
SO MUCH OF MY WORK

81
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:25,956
THEY'D FIRE ME.

82
00:03:25,956 --> 00:03:29,918
SO? THEN YOU COULD STAY
AS LONG AS YOU WANT.

83
00:03:29,918 --> 00:03:32,211
I WISH I COULD.

84
00:03:32,211 --> 00:03:35,841
OH, DON'T-DON'T
START PACKING.

85
00:03:35,841 --> 00:03:40,220
COME ON.

86
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,972
I DON'T THINK
YOU UNDERSTAND PACKING.

87
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:46,351
I DON'T WANT TO LEAVE IT
TILL THE LAST MINUTE.

88
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:48,937
THE LAST TIME I PACKED
IN A RUSH, I LEFT MY KNICKERS.

89
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:52,774
YEAH, I KNOW.
I, UH, I TRIED THEM ON.

90
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:53,942
YOU DIDN'T!

91
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,110
NO, I DIDN'T.

92
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:56,695
I DIDN'T WANT TO BE THAT GUY.

93
00:04:00,239 --> 00:04:02,450
( karate yells )

94
00:04:05,829 --> 00:04:07,455
HELLO.

95
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:12,127
HO, HO, HO!

96
00:04:12,127 --> 00:04:13,170
EXCUSE ME?

97
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:14,462
YOUR PANTS.

98
00:04:14,462 --> 00:04:15,589
OH, YEAH!

99
00:04:15,589 --> 00:04:17,174
YOU LIKE THEM?

100
00:04:17,174 --> 00:04:18,508
I WENT TO
A USED CLOTHES STORE

101
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:20,677
AND GOT A BUNCH
OF MATERNITY STUFF.

102
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:22,846
THESE ARE SO COMFORTABLE.

103
00:04:25,933 --> 00:04:30,478
UH, PHEEBS,
THOSE ARE SANTA PANTS.

104
00:04:30,478 --> 00:04:31,605
WHAT?

105
00:04:31,605 --> 00:04:33,774
SANTA PANTS.

106
00:04:33,774 --> 00:04:37,069
SANTA CLAUS'S PANTS.

107
00:04:37,069 --> 00:04:39,154
NUH-UH.
THEY'RE MATERNITY PANTS.

108
00:04:39,154 --> 00:04:42,157
THEY EVEN CAME
WITH A LIST OF BABY NAMES.

109
00:04:42,157 --> 00:04:43,533
SEE?

110
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:47,996
THESE NAMES ARE GOOD
AND THESE ARE BAD.

111
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:50,582
OH.

112
00:04:50,582 --> 00:04:51,583
HEY.

113
00:04:51,583 --> 00:04:52,667
HEY.

114
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:54,711
HEY, PHEEBS.

115
00:04:54,711 --> 00:04:58,215
SO, HOW ARE THE ELVES?

116
00:04:58,215 --> 00:04:59,216
( goofy voice ):
I DON'T KNOW.

117
00:04:59,216 --> 00:05:00,759
HOW ARE THE...

118
00:05:00,759 --> 00:05:02,052
YOU KNOW.

119
00:05:03,929 --> 00:05:05,055
YOUR CLOTHES AREN'T FUNNY.

120
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:10,769
HEY, GUYS, WHAT SHOULD
I WEAR TO A KNICKS GAME?

121
00:05:10,769 --> 00:05:13,147
UH, A T-SHIRT THAT SAYS,
"I DON'T BELONG HERE."

122
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:16,775
YOU HAVE KNICKS TICKETS?

123
00:05:16,775 --> 00:05:18,068
YEAH. MY MOM
GOT MY DAD'S

124
00:05:18,068 --> 00:05:19,444
SEASON TICKETS
IN THE DIVORCE

125
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:20,946
SO SHE JUST
GAVE THEM TO ME.

126
00:05:20,946 --> 00:05:23,615
APPARENTLY, THEY'RE
PRETTY GOOD SEATS.

127
00:05:23,615 --> 00:05:25,993
OH, MY GOD!
THOSE ARE ALMOST
RIGHT ON THE FLOOR!

128
00:05:25,993 --> 00:05:28,703
DO YOU GUYS WANT THESE?

129
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:30,789
YEAH!
YEAH, WE DO!

130
00:05:30,789 --> 00:05:31,873
OH, WELL, YOU GOT 'EM.

131
00:05:31,873 --> 00:05:33,125
ALL RIGHT!

132
00:05:33,125 --> 00:05:34,668
JUST GIVE US
OUR APARTMENT BACK.

133
00:05:38,797 --> 00:05:40,715
WHOA! I DIDN'T
SEE THAT COMING.

134
00:05:42,676 --> 00:05:44,178
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

135
00:05:44,178 --> 00:05:45,637
( taunting ):
COME ON.

136
00:05:45,637 --> 00:05:47,889
WE KNOW WHAT
THESE ARE WORTH.

137
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:51,018
WHAT, DO YOU THINK
WE'RE STUPID?
NOT STUPID.

138
00:05:51,018 --> 00:05:54,021
YOU'RE MEANER
THAN I THOUGHT.

139
00:05:54,021 --> 00:05:55,022
WHAT DO YOU SAY?

140
00:05:55,022 --> 00:05:56,397
FORGET IT, OKAY?

141
00:05:56,397 --> 00:05:58,399
I'M NOT GIVING UP
MY BACHELOR PAD

142
00:05:58,399 --> 00:06:00,068
FOR SOME BASKETBALL SEATS.

143
00:06:00,068 --> 00:06:02,821
YOUR BACHELOR PAD?

144
00:06:02,821 --> 00:06:04,781
HAVE YOU EVEN HAD
A GIRL UP HERE?

145
00:06:07,408 --> 00:06:09,494
NO.

146
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:11,038
BUT, UH... JOEY HAS

147
00:06:11,038 --> 00:06:13,165
AND I USUALLY TALK TO THEM
IN THE MORNING TIME.

148
00:06:15,834 --> 00:06:17,127
YEAH, YOU DO.

149
00:06:23,508 --> 00:06:25,260
COME ON.

150
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:28,763
YES, GUNTHER, CAN I GET
TWO CUPS OF CHINO, PLEASE?

151
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:31,225
GOOD ONE.

152
00:06:31,225 --> 00:06:32,726
HEY, COME ON--
SEASON TICKETS.

153
00:06:32,726 --> 00:06:35,312
SEASON TICKETS.
YOU KNOW WHAT THAT MEANS?

154
00:06:35,312 --> 00:06:38,023
FORGET IT. I'M NOT
GIVING UP THE APARTMENT.

155
00:06:38,023 --> 00:06:39,440
LOOK, WHEN I WAS
A LITTLE KID

156
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,109
MY DAD'S COMPANY GAVE
SEASON TICKETS

157
00:06:41,109 --> 00:06:43,737
TO THE NUMBER-ONE
SALESMAN EVERY YEAR.

158
00:06:43,737 --> 00:06:46,323
MY DAD NEVER WON.

159
00:06:46,323 --> 00:06:47,782
OF COURSE, HE WASN'T
IN THE SALES DIVISION

160
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:50,618
BUT STILL, I NEVER
EVER, EVER FORGOT THAT.

161
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:52,871
HEY, GUYS.

162
00:06:52,871 --> 00:06:53,872
HEY.

163
00:06:53,872 --> 00:06:58,043
OH, MY GOD.

164
00:06:58,043 --> 00:07:01,420
WE DON'T MAKE ENOUGH
FUN OF YOU ALREADY?

165
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:04,507
OH, YEAH.
EMILY CONVINCED
ME TO DO IT.

166
00:07:04,507 --> 00:07:07,094
YOU DO KNOW
THAT WHAM! BROKE UP?

167
00:07:07,094 --> 00:07:10,722
( laughing )

168
00:07:10,722 --> 00:07:12,557
YEAH, WELL, I LIKE IT
AND EMILY LIKES IT

169
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:13,516
AND THAT'S WHAT COUNTS.

170
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:18,479
SO, UH, HOW ARE
YOU GUYS DOING?

171
00:07:18,479 --> 00:07:19,480
DON'T TRY AND
TALK ALL NORMAL

172
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,609
WITH THAT THING
IN YOUR EAR.

173
00:07:22,609 --> 00:07:24,527
WHERE'S EMILY?

174
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:26,445
SHE'S SAYING GOOD-BYE
TO HER UNCLE.

175
00:07:26,445 --> 00:07:28,489
MAN, DIDN'T SHE, LIKE,
JUST GET HERE?

176
00:07:28,489 --> 00:07:30,242
YEAH! YEAH!

177
00:07:30,242 --> 00:07:32,369
EASY, TIGER.

178
00:07:32,369 --> 00:07:34,454
I JUST... I HATE THIS SO MUCH.

179
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:36,539
EVERY TIME I GO PICK HER UP
AT THE AIRPORT

180
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:39,251
IT'S SO GREAT,
BUT AT THE SAME TIME

181
00:07:39,251 --> 00:07:41,128
I'M THINKING, WELL, I'M GOING
TO BE RIGHT BACK THERE

182
00:07:41,128 --> 00:07:43,630
IN A COUPLE OF DAYS
DROPPING HER OFF.

183
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:44,672
WHAT ARE YOU
GOING TO DO?

184
00:07:44,672 --> 00:07:45,924
THERE'S NOTHING TO DO.

185
00:07:45,924 --> 00:07:47,717
SHE LIVES THERE, I LIVE HERE.

186
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:50,678
I MEAN, SHE'D HAVE TO MOVE HERE.

187
00:07:50,678 --> 00:07:53,598
SHE SHOULD MOVE HERE.

188
00:07:53,598 --> 00:07:54,891
WHAT?

189
00:07:54,891 --> 00:07:56,310
I COULD ASK HER
TO LIVE WITH ME.

190
00:07:56,310 --> 00:07:57,436
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

191
00:07:57,436 --> 00:07:58,979
WHY NOT? I MEAN, WHY NOT?

192
00:07:58,979 --> 00:08:00,939
BECAUSE YOU'VE
ONLY KNOWN HER SIX WEEKS.

193
00:08:00,939 --> 00:08:02,649
I'VE GOT A CARTON OF MILK
IN MY REFRIGERATOR

194
00:08:02,649 --> 00:08:06,027
I'VE HAD A LONGER
RELATIONSHIP WITH.

195
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:09,614
BUT, GUYS, WHEN I'M
WITH HER, IT'S LIKE...

196
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:13,285
SHE BRINGS OUT
THIS-THIS THIS GREAT SIDE OF ME.

197
00:08:13,285 --> 00:08:16,079
I MEAN, I LOVE HER, YOU KNOW?

198
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:18,290
AND I LOVE THE MILK!

199
00:08:18,290 --> 00:08:19,498
BUT I'M NOT GOING TO ASK

200
00:08:19,498 --> 00:08:21,251
SOME BRITISH GIRL
TO MOVE IN WITH ME.

201
00:08:26,673 --> 00:08:30,135
JOEY, YOU SAY
THINGS NOW.

202
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:32,179
LOOK, ROSS, HE'S RIGHT.

203
00:08:32,179 --> 00:08:33,388
EMILY IS GREAT.

204
00:08:33,388 --> 00:08:34,389
SHE'S GREAT

205
00:08:34,389 --> 00:08:36,016
BUT THIS IS TOO SOON.

206
00:08:36,016 --> 00:08:38,352
YOU'RE ONLY GOING TO SCARE HER.

207
00:08:38,352 --> 00:08:39,727
I DON'T WANT TO DO THAT.
NO.

208
00:08:39,727 --> 00:08:40,854
YOU DON'T WANT
TO WRECK IT.

209
00:08:40,854 --> 00:08:43,482
YOU DON'T WANT
TO GO TOO FAST.

210
00:08:43,482 --> 00:08:44,565
YEAH. NO,
YOU'RE RIGHT.

211
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:45,984
I KNOW YOU'RE RIGHT.

212
00:08:45,984 --> 00:08:49,237
I'M NOT GOING
TO DO IT.

213
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:50,364
THANKS, GUYS.

214
00:08:50,364 --> 00:08:51,739
OKAY, NO PROBLEM.

215
00:08:51,739 --> 00:08:55,535
JUST REMEMBER TO WAKE US UP
BEFORE YOU GO-GO.

216
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:09,299
OH, IT'S TOO HARD.
TOO HARD!

217
00:09:09,299 --> 00:09:10,509
ALL RIGHT, BOYS--

218
00:09:10,509 --> 00:09:12,219
LAST CHANCE
FOR THE TICKETS.

219
00:09:12,219 --> 00:09:14,888
OTHERWISE, I GIVE THEM
TO MY NEW BOYFRIEND JOSHUA.

220
00:09:17,391 --> 00:09:19,309
NO, THANK YOU.

221
00:09:19,309 --> 00:09:20,560
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT,
WAIT, WAIT.

222
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,396
COME ON, COME ON--
LET'S TRADE.

223
00:09:22,396 --> 00:09:23,480
THE TIMING'S PERFECT.

224
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:27,942
I JUST CLOGGED THE TOILET!

225
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:29,319
LOOK, I WANT THOSE
BASKETBALL SEATS

226
00:09:29,319 --> 00:09:30,904
AS MUCH AS YOU DO, OKAY?

227
00:09:30,904 --> 00:09:31,905
BUT WE CAN'T LIVE IN
THE SMALL APARTMENT

228
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:33,573
AFTER WE'VE LIVED HERE!

229
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:35,075
DIDN'T YOU EVER READ
FLOWERS FOR ALGERNON?

230
00:09:35,075 --> 00:09:37,411
YES...

231
00:09:37,411 --> 00:09:39,079
DIDN'T YOU EVER READ
SPORTS ILLUSTRATED?

232
00:09:41,164 --> 00:09:43,417
NO, I DIDN'T READ YOURS.

233
00:09:43,417 --> 00:09:45,001
LOOK, COME ON, WE CAN GO
TO THE GAME TONIGHT.

234
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:47,546
LOOK, THE ONLY WAY I
WILL EVEN CONSIDER THIS

235
00:09:47,546 --> 00:09:50,215
IS IF THEY OFFER A LOT MORE
THAN JUST SEASON SEATS.

236
00:09:50,215 --> 00:09:51,383
BUT IT'S THE KNICKS!

237
00:09:51,383 --> 00:09:53,593
SCREW THE KNICKS!
WHOA...

238
00:09:58,139 --> 00:10:00,225
I DIDN'T MEAN THAT.

239
00:10:00,225 --> 00:10:04,812
I JUST MEANT
THAT THE APARTMENT
IS WORTH SO MUCH MORE.

240
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:07,857
HUH.

241
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:09,067
AND THE KNICKS RULE ALL.

242
00:10:09,067 --> 00:10:11,986
YEAH! THE KNICKS
RULE ALL.

243
00:10:11,986 --> 00:10:13,988
HEY, SO ARE YOU
GOING TO DO IT?

244
00:10:13,988 --> 00:10:16,991
NO. NO, WE'RE NOT.
YOU KNOW WHY?

245
00:10:16,991 --> 00:10:18,452
BECAUSE IT'S NOT
AN EVEN TRADE.

246
00:10:18,452 --> 00:10:21,871
LOOK, WHAT IF YOU COULD
KEEP THE APARTMENT

247
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:22,914
AND GET THE TICKETS?

248
00:10:22,914 --> 00:10:24,707
DONE!

249
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:26,501
LET ME FINISH.

250
00:10:26,501 --> 00:10:28,336
WE'RE TALKING
ABOUT A BET--
WINNER TAKES ALL.

251
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:29,754
WE COULD END UP
WITH NOTHING.

252
00:10:29,754 --> 00:10:31,256
OR END UP WITH
EVERYTHING.

253
00:10:31,256 --> 00:10:32,549
OOH, I LIKE THAT.

254
00:10:34,008 --> 00:10:35,635
ALL RIGHT,
SO WHAT DO YOU SAY?

255
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:37,637
NO!
OH, JUST DO IT!

256
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:39,306
OH! OH, I'M CONVINCED.

257
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:42,517
COME ON, MAN.

258
00:10:42,517 --> 00:10:44,394
YOU KNOW
I'D DO IT FOR YOU.

259
00:10:44,394 --> 00:10:46,354
BECAUSE YOU'RE
MY BEST FRIEND.

260
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:47,814
( sighing )

261
00:10:47,814 --> 00:10:49,732
ALL RIGHT, BUT YOU
CAN'T USE THAT AGAIN

262
00:10:49,732 --> 00:10:51,985
FOR A WHOLE YEAR.

263
00:10:51,985 --> 00:10:53,111
I'M IN.

264
00:10:53,111 --> 00:10:56,072
OOH! THIS
IS SO EXCITING!

265
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:57,949
OH, GOD, WHAT
ARE YOU GOING TO BET?

266
00:10:57,949 --> 00:11:00,034
OH, OKAY. WELL,
I THINK WE SHOULD
LET PHOEBE DECIDE

267
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:01,702
BECAUSE SHE'S THE ONLY ONE
WHO'S IMPARTIAL

268
00:11:01,702 --> 00:11:05,582
AND SHE'S SO PRETTY.

269
00:11:05,582 --> 00:11:06,665
OKAY.

270
00:11:06,665 --> 00:11:08,376
UM... OOH, OOH...

271
00:11:08,376 --> 00:11:09,586
OH, I HAVE A GAME!

272
00:11:09,586 --> 00:11:11,087
OH, THIS IS GREAT!

273
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:12,297
WHAT'S THE GAME,
WHAT'S THE GAME?

274
00:11:12,297 --> 00:11:14,007
WELL,
IT DOESN'T HAVE A NAME.

275
00:11:14,007 --> 00:11:15,800
NO, OKAY: "PHOEBE BALL."

276
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,302
( chuckling )

277
00:11:17,302 --> 00:11:19,304
NO, IT DOESN'T
HAVE A NAME.

278
00:11:19,304 --> 00:11:24,309
UM... OKAY, MONICA,
WHAT IS YOUR FAVORITE THING

279
00:11:24,309 --> 00:11:26,394
ABOUT TREES?

280
00:11:28,522 --> 00:11:30,940
THEY'RE GREEN?
GOOD! GOOD!
FIVE POINTS!

281
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:32,609
ALL RIGHT!

282
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:35,694
Phoebe:
GREAT! ALL RIGHT

283
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:37,197
JOEY...

284
00:11:37,197 --> 00:11:40,699
SAME QUESTION.

285
00:11:40,699 --> 00:11:42,202
UH...
OH!

286
00:11:42,202 --> 00:11:43,495
HMM. THEY'RE TALL.

287
00:11:43,495 --> 00:11:44,829
OOH! THREE POINTS.

288
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:48,707
NO. BOTH FINE ANSWERS

289
00:11:48,707 --> 00:11:50,502
BUT WE WERE LOOKING
FOR "LEAFY."

290
00:11:50,502 --> 00:11:52,086
"LEAFY."

291
00:11:54,506 --> 00:11:56,132
THAT'S NOT EVEN A GAME.

292
00:11:56,132 --> 00:11:59,802
SHUT UP!
WE'RE WINNING.

293
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,429
YOU WANT TO FINISH
THIS RIGHT NOW?

294
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:02,681
WE GET A DECK
OF CARDS.

295
00:12:02,681 --> 00:12:04,391
HIGH CARD WINS.
WHAT DO YOU SAY?

296
00:12:04,391 --> 00:12:05,559
FINE. LET'S DO IT.

297
00:12:05,559 --> 00:12:07,143
OOH! I HAVE CARDS.
OH, GOOD.

298
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:08,727
YEAH! HERE.

299
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:10,438
OH, NO. THESE
ARE THE TRICK DECK.

300
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:13,941
OKAY... HERE, YES.
OKAY.

301
00:12:13,941 --> 00:12:15,026
OKAY, YOU GUYS...
YOU GUYS PICK FIRST.

302
00:12:15,026 --> 00:12:15,985
OKAY.

303
00:12:20,865 --> 00:12:23,284
FOUR.
THAT'S A
LOW ONE-NAH!

304
00:12:25,078 --> 00:12:26,538
ALL RIGHT.

305
00:12:26,538 --> 00:12:28,623
PHOEBE, YOU LOOK.
I CAN'T DO IT.

306
00:12:28,623 --> 00:12:30,458
WHAT MAKES YOU THINK
I CAN?!

307
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:31,459
OKAY, OKAY.

308
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:32,793
ACE!

309
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:37,756
( screaming )
( screaming )

310
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:39,133
WHY ARE YOU SCREAMING
AND HUGGING?

311
00:12:39,133 --> 00:12:40,552
WE WON OUR
APARTMENT BACK!

312
00:12:40,552 --> 00:12:41,720
Joey:
WHAT?

313
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:44,347
ACE IS HIGH:
JACK, QUEEN, KING, ACE.

314
00:12:44,347 --> 00:12:47,183
NO, ACE IS LOW: ACE,
TWO, THREE, FOUR.

315
00:12:55,024 --> 00:12:56,359
I DON'T KNOW.

316
00:12:56,359 --> 00:12:58,570
BUT, BUT, OOH!

317
00:12:58,570 --> 00:13:00,113
OOH!

318
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:02,031
LOOKIT! AH!

319
00:13:04,451 --> 00:13:05,910
PICK AGAIN,
PICK AGAIN!

320
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:07,287
ALL RIGHT, GIMME, GIMME.

321
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:09,122
OKAY.
OKAY.

322
00:13:09,122 --> 00:13:10,248
COME ON,
APARTMENT!

323
00:13:10,248 --> 00:13:12,166
COME ON, APARTMENT!

324
00:13:12,166 --> 00:13:14,377
( sighing )

325
00:13:14,377 --> 00:13:15,503
( whooping )

326
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:17,631
I KNOW QUEEN IS HIGH!

327
00:13:17,631 --> 00:13:20,341
AH, NOT AS HIGH AS...

328
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:21,968
IT WORKED! KING!

329
00:13:21,968 --> 00:13:23,344
WE WIN!
( laughing )

330
00:13:23,344 --> 00:13:25,472
( whooping )

331
00:13:25,472 --> 00:13:26,973
WE PICK AGAIN,
WE PICK AGAIN!

332
00:13:26,973 --> 00:13:28,558
WHY?
I DON'T KNOW.

333
00:13:30,644 --> 00:13:32,061
TICKETS, PLEASE.

334
00:13:32,061 --> 00:13:34,397
( frustrated groan )

335
00:13:34,397 --> 00:13:36,608
THAT'S COURTSIDE, BABY!

336
00:13:36,608 --> 00:13:37,816
( laughing ):
YEAH!

337
00:13:37,816 --> 00:13:39,026
SERIOUSLY, GOOD
GAME, THOUGH!

338
00:13:39,026 --> 00:13:40,194
GOOD GAME...

339
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:43,197
WHAT ARE THEY
SO MAD ABOUT?

340
00:13:43,197 --> 00:13:44,699
THEY GOT THE
APARTMENT BACK.

341
00:13:46,409 --> 00:13:47,702
NO, THEY DIDN'T.

342
00:13:47,702 --> 00:13:50,037
( door opens and shuts )

343
00:13:56,169 --> 00:13:57,504
HEY.

344
00:13:57,504 --> 00:14:00,173
PACKED WHILE
YOU WERE GONE.

345
00:14:00,173 --> 00:14:02,634
I LEFT SOME KNICKERS
UNDER YOUR PILLOW.

346
00:14:04,594 --> 00:14:07,221
MOVE IN WITH ME.

347
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:08,348
WHAT?

348
00:14:08,348 --> 00:14:09,724
DON'T BE SCARED.

349
00:14:09,724 --> 00:14:11,017
I-I KNOW IT SOUNDS CRAZY

350
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:13,144
AND PEOPLE WILL SAY
IT'S TOO SOON

351
00:14:13,144 --> 00:14:15,396
BUT JUST, JUST THINK.

352
00:14:15,396 --> 00:14:17,816
THINK HOW GREAT IT WOULD BE.

353
00:14:18,857 --> 00:14:20,026
OH...

354
00:14:20,026 --> 00:14:22,487
I DON'T KNOW.

355
00:14:22,487 --> 00:14:23,655
( sighing )

356
00:14:23,655 --> 00:14:25,573
OH, LEAVING LONDON. UH...

357
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:27,826
MY WHOLE FAMILY
LIVES THERE.

358
00:14:27,826 --> 00:14:29,076
MY JOB.

359
00:14:29,076 --> 00:14:30,453
WELL, SO YOU'LL GET
A JOB HERE.

360
00:14:30,453 --> 00:14:32,205
I MEAN, I'M ALWAYS HEARING

361
00:14:32,205 --> 00:14:34,915
ABOUT THEM FOREIGNERS COMING IN
AND STEALING AMERICAN JOBS.

362
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:37,669
THAT COULD BE YOU.

363
00:14:37,669 --> 00:14:39,212
YEAH, BUT I-IT'S
MY WHOLE LIFE.

364
00:14:40,714 --> 00:14:41,840
YOU COME TO ENGLAND.

365
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:43,174
NO, I CAN'T.

366
00:14:43,174 --> 00:14:45,301
I WOULD, I REALLY WOULD,
BUT MY SON IS HERE.

367
00:14:45,301 --> 00:14:47,637
I CAN'T LEAVE HIM.

368
00:14:47,637 --> 00:14:49,305
YOU DON'T THINK
THERE'S ANY WAY?

369
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:54,227
OH, I DON'T THINK SO.

370
00:14:54,227 --> 00:14:57,271
I MEAN, IT WOULD BE DIFFERENT
IF IT WAS WAY INTO THE FUTURE

371
00:14:57,271 --> 00:15:00,149
AND, AND WE WERE GETTING
MARRIED, OR SOMETHING.

372
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:01,150
WHAT?

373
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:02,485
OH. NO. NO, RIGHT.

374
00:15:02,485 --> 00:15:04,863
UH, I SHOULDN'T HAVE
SAID "MARRIED."

375
00:15:04,863 --> 00:15:07,114
UH, PLEASE DON'T
GET FREAKY ON ME.

376
00:15:07,114 --> 00:15:10,076
UH... I DIDN'T
MEAN IT.

377
00:15:10,076 --> 00:15:11,077
I TAKE IT BACK.

378
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:12,161
NO, NO, DON'T.

379
00:15:14,581 --> 00:15:16,957
WHY DON'T WE?

380
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:18,042
WHY DON'T WE WHAT?

381
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:20,503
( nervous laugh )

382
00:15:20,503 --> 00:15:22,046
GET MARRIED.

383
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:24,632
YOU ARE MAD.

384
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:26,092
NO, NO!
I'M NOT.

385
00:15:26,092 --> 00:15:27,802
IT'S-IT'S-IT'S PERFECT!

386
00:15:27,802 --> 00:15:30,012
I MEAN, IT'S BETTER
THAN YOU JUST MOVING HERE

387
00:15:30,012 --> 00:15:31,264
'CAUSE IT'S US
TOGETHER FOREVER

388
00:15:31,264 --> 00:15:33,474
AND THAT'S,
THAT'S WHAT I WANT.

389
00:15:33,474 --> 00:15:35,560
WE'VE ONLY KNOWN EACH
OTHER FOR SIX WEEKS.

390
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:36,561
I KNOW. SO WHAT?

391
00:15:36,561 --> 00:15:37,854
I MEAN, WHO'S TO SAY?

392
00:15:37,854 --> 00:15:39,856
DOES THAT MEAN
WE, WE CAN'T DO IT?

393
00:15:39,856 --> 00:15:42,901
LOOK, I WAS WITH CAROL
FOR FOUR YEARS

394
00:15:42,901 --> 00:15:44,318
BEFORE WE GOT MARRIED

395
00:15:44,318 --> 00:15:47,488
AND I WOUND UP DIVORCED
FROM A PREGNANT LESBIAN.

396
00:15:49,908 --> 00:15:52,368
I MEAN, THIS...

397
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:55,914
THIS MAKES SENSE FOR US.

398
00:15:55,914 --> 00:15:57,957
COME ON!
I MEAN, OUR FIRST DATE

399
00:15:57,957 --> 00:16:00,543
WE ENDED UP SPENDING
THE WHOLE WEEKEND IN VERMONT.

400
00:16:00,543 --> 00:16:02,796
I MEAN, LAST NIGHT,
I GOT MY EAR PIERCED.

401
00:16:02,796 --> 00:16:03,797
ME!

402
00:16:03,797 --> 00:16:05,381
( laughing )

403
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:07,508
IT JUST FEELS RIGHT.

404
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:08,927
DOESN'T IT?

405
00:16:10,553 --> 00:16:13,139
MY PARENTS ARE GOING
TO BE REALLY MAD.

406
00:16:13,139 --> 00:16:15,057
IS THAT...
ARE YOU SAYING "YES"?

407
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:16,058
IS THAT "YES"?

408
00:16:16,058 --> 00:16:17,769
YES.

409
00:16:20,313 --> 00:16:21,439
YES!

410
00:16:21,439 --> 00:16:22,816
YES? WE'RE GETTING...?

411
00:16:22,816 --> 00:16:23,858
WE'RE GETTING MARRIED?

412
00:16:23,858 --> 00:16:25,652
OH, MY GOD!

413
00:16:25,652 --> 00:16:27,320
WE'RE GETTING MARRIED!

414
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,488
WE, WE...

415
00:16:28,488 --> 00:16:30,657
COME HERE, COME HERE.

416
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,371
OW!

417
00:16:40,667 --> 00:16:42,168
EMILY, WILL YOU MARRY ME?

418
00:16:44,253 --> 00:16:45,296
YES.

419
00:16:49,175 --> 00:16:52,303
OH, IT'S A BIT SMALL.

420
00:16:52,303 --> 00:16:54,973
DAMN! I THOUGHT THAT WAS GOING
TO BE ROMANTIC AS HELL!

421
00:16:58,476 --> 00:16:59,602
IT WAS.

422
00:17:13,199 --> 00:17:15,284
THOSE WERE, LIKE,
THE BEST SEATS EVER.

423
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:18,621
OH, YEAH. HEY!
SHOULD WE GIVE THESE
SHIRTS TO THE GIRLS

424
00:17:18,621 --> 00:17:20,456
YOU KNOW, KIND OF LIKE
A PEACE OFFERING?

425
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:22,040
YEAH. THAT'S VERY NICE.

426
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:23,417
PLUS, THEY WERE FREE
AND THEY'RE TOO SMALL.

427
00:17:28,965 --> 00:17:30,424
OH... OH, GOD!

428
00:17:37,097 --> 00:17:38,265
HEY, YOU WANT
A BEER?

429
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:41,895
WHOA!

430
00:17:41,895 --> 00:17:43,021
I KNOW!

431
00:17:46,691 --> 00:17:49,151
OPEN UP! OPEN UP! OPEN UP!

432
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:52,238
WE'LL DISCUSS IT
IN THE MORNING.

433
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:03,332
WHAT THE HELL IS GOING ON?

434
00:18:03,332 --> 00:18:05,919
WE TOOK OUR
APARTMENT BACK.

435
00:18:09,255 --> 00:18:11,257
I HAD NOTHING
TO DO WITH IT.

436
00:18:14,761 --> 00:18:16,136
OKAY. IT WAS MY IDEA

437
00:18:16,136 --> 00:18:19,057
BUT I DON'T FEEL
GOOD ABOUT IT.

438
00:18:19,057 --> 00:18:20,182
OH! OH!

439
00:18:21,642 --> 00:18:24,311
WE ARE SWITCHING BACK
RIGHT NOW.

440
00:18:24,311 --> 00:18:27,023
NO, WE'RE NOT.
WE'RE NOT LEAVING.

441
00:18:27,023 --> 00:18:28,232
WELL, YOU'RE GOING
TO HAVE TO LEAVE SOMETIME

442
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:29,734
BECAUSE YOU BOTH
HAVE JOBS

443
00:18:29,734 --> 00:18:31,861
AND AS SOON AS YOU DO,
WE'RE SWITCHING IT BACK.

444
00:18:31,861 --> 00:18:35,073
THERE'S NOTHING YOU CAN DO
TO STOP US, RIGHT, JOE?

445
00:18:35,073 --> 00:18:40,078
I DON'T KNOW. I...

446
00:18:40,078 --> 00:18:41,621
WHAT?!

447
00:18:41,621 --> 00:18:42,914
I DON'T WANT TO MOVE AGAIN.

448
00:18:42,914 --> 00:18:45,750
( mumbling )

449
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:47,126
I DON'T CARE.

450
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:48,920
THIS IS OUR APARTMENT
AND THEY STOLE--

451
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:52,381
YOU STOLE!--
OUR APARTMENT.

452
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:54,801
WE WON THAT APARTMENT
FAIR AND SQUARE TWICE

453
00:18:54,801 --> 00:18:56,176
AND I AM GETTING
IT BACK RIGHT NOW.

454
00:18:56,176 --> 00:19:00,264
I'M GETTING IT
BACK RIGHT NOW!

455
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:02,433
ALL RIGHT...

456
00:19:02,433 --> 00:19:05,561
WE FIGURED YOU MIGHT
RESPOND THIS WAY

457
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:07,063
SO WE HAVE
A BACKUP OFFER.

458
00:19:07,063 --> 00:19:08,522
OH, NO, NO, NO.
NO MORE OFFERS.

459
00:19:08,522 --> 00:19:10,149
YOU CAN'T OFFER
ANYTHING TO US.

460
00:19:10,149 --> 00:19:13,277
LET US KEEP THE
APARTMENT AND...

461
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:14,612
AS A THANK YOU...

462
00:19:18,032 --> 00:19:19,784
RACHEL AND I WILL KISS
FOR ONE MINUTE.

463
00:19:24,789 --> 00:19:26,499
TOTALLY WORTH IT.

464
00:19:26,499 --> 00:19:27,667
THAT WAS ONE
GOOD MINUTE.

465
00:19:27,667 --> 00:19:29,961
GOOD NIGHT.
GOOD NIGHT.

466
00:19:34,882 --> 00:19:37,593
MEN ARE SUCH IDIOTS.

467
00:19:37,593 --> 00:19:39,553
I KNOW. CAN YOU BELIEVE
SOMETHING THAT STUPID

468
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:42,056
ACTUALLY GOT US
OUR APARTMENT BACK?

469
00:19:42,056 --> 00:19:43,557
IT'S SO FUNNY TO THINK--

470
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:45,935
IF YOU HAD JUST DONE THAT
AFTER THE LAST CONTEST

471
00:19:45,935 --> 00:19:48,104
NO ONE WOULD'VE HAD
TO MOVE AT ALL.

472
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:52,984
L-L-LET'S PRETEND
THAT'S NOT TRUE.

473
00:19:52,984 --> 00:19:54,485
YEAH.

474
00:19:56,029 --> 00:19:59,532
OKAY... SCARF'S DONE.

475
00:20:02,284 --> 00:20:03,285
COME ON, COME ON, COME ON.

476
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:04,996
OKAY.

477
00:20:04,996 --> 00:20:05,997
HI.

478
00:20:05,997 --> 00:20:06,998
HEY.
HEY.

479
00:20:06,998 --> 00:20:08,415
WHAT'S GOING ON?

480
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:10,751
ROSS HAS SOME
BIG THING TO
TELL EVERYONE.

481
00:20:10,751 --> 00:20:13,587
UH... UH, OKAY...

482
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:15,089
IT'S, UH...

483
00:20:15,089 --> 00:20:16,340
EMILY AND I...

484
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:18,801
WE DECIDED TO, UH...
TO GET MARRIED.

485
00:20:22,596 --> 00:20:24,223
WHAT?!

486
00:20:24,223 --> 00:20:28,102
OH! ARE YOU PREGNANT, TOO?

487
00:20:28,102 --> 00:20:30,146
UH, NO.

488
00:20:30,146 --> 00:20:31,480
WHEN... WHEN DID...?

489
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,232
HOW... HOW DID YOU...?

490
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:36,569
WE-WE JUST DECIDED
TO... TO GO FOR IT.

491
00:20:36,569 --> 00:20:38,029
I MEAN, WE KNOW
IT'S A BIT HASTY

492
00:20:38,029 --> 00:20:39,780
BUT, UH...

493
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:43,034
IT JUST FEELS SO RIGHT, SO...

494
00:20:46,829 --> 00:20:48,831
UM... I WAS JUST TELLING
THE GUYS...

495
00:20:48,831 --> 00:20:51,167
YEAH. I... I HEARD.

496
00:20:57,131 --> 00:20:59,759
I THINK IT'S GREAT!

497
00:20:59,759 --> 00:21:01,343
I'M SO HAPPY FOR YOU.

498
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:03,096
WELL, YEAH... CONGRATULATIONS.

499
00:21:03,096 --> 00:21:04,055
OH, YEAH, YEAH.

500
00:21:06,057 --> 00:21:07,725
OH, MY GOD.

501
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:13,689
I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU'RE GETTING MARRIED.

502
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:14,982
YEAH.

503
00:21:18,569 --> 00:21:20,947
MONICA AND RACHEL
MADE OUT.

504
00:21:31,582 --> 00:21:35,586
Singing Guy:
♪ MORNING'S HERE ♪

505
00:21:35,586 --> 00:21:38,631
♪ THE MORNING'S HERE ♪

506
00:21:38,631 --> 00:21:41,300
Both:
♪ SUNSHINE IS HERE ♪

507
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:43,010
♪ THE SKY IS CLEAR ♪

508
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,054
♪ THE MORNING'S HERE... ♪

509
00:21:45,054 --> 00:21:46,139
HEY! YOU'RE BACK!

510
00:21:46,139 --> 00:21:48,474
HEY!
♪ GET INTO GEAR ♪

511
00:21:48,474 --> 00:21:50,851
♪ BREAKFAST IS NEAR ♪

512
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:55,606
♪ THE DARK OF NIGHT
HAS DISAPPEARED ♪

513
00:21:55,606 --> 00:21:58,943
I'LL SEE YOU
TOMORROW MORNING.
OKAY.

